@Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5056
@userId = alice
@callType = development
@callId = team-standup

### Issue a Stream user token (creates the user if missing; only sent fields are updated)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Alice",
  "image": "https://getstream.io/random_png/?name=Alice"
}

### Refresh a token (userId only; leaves the existing user unchanged)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}"
}

### Invalid request: returns 400 ValidationProblem
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "bad id!",
  "image": "ftp://example.com/alice.png"
}

### Create a call (the server creates calls; the browser joins them)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "{{callType}}",
  "id": "{{callId}}",
  "createdById": "{{userId}}",
  "members": [
    { "userId": "bob", "role": "host" }
  ]
}

### Get one call
GET {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}

### List calls
GET {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls?type={{callType}}&limit=10

### Add and remove members
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "add": [ { "userId": "carol" } ],
  "remove": [ "bob" ]
}

### Start recording (409 until someone has joined the call)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}/recordings/start

### Stop recording
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}/recordings/stop

### List recordings (appear once Stream finishes processing)
GET {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}/recordings

### End the call for everyone
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/calls/{{callType}}/{{callId}}/end

### Consultation: patient taps "Call now" (copy the callId from the response)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "patient-001",
  "modality": "video",
  "reason": "sore throat for three days"
}

### Dispatch board: who is waiting
GET {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations?status=waiting

@consultationId = replace-with-callId-from-the-create-response

### Triage picks it up (triage only; patients and doctors get 403)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations/{{consultationId}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffId": "triage-001"
}

### Bring a doctor into the live call (adds them, then rings them)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations/{{consultationId}}/invite
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doctorId": "doctor-001"
}

### Ring that doctor again
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations/{{consultationId}}/ring
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doctorId": "doctor-001"
}

### Finish the consultation
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations/{{consultationId}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffId": "triage-001"
}

### Patient gives up while waiting (only from waiting, only the owning patient)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/consultations/{{consultationId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "patient-001"
}

### Webhook with an invalid signature: returns 401 (Stream signs real ones)
POST {{Amt.GetStream.Api_HostAddress}}/api/webhooks/stream
Content-Type: application/json
X-Signature: not-a-valid-signature

{
  "type": "call.ended",
  "call_cid": "{{callType}}:{{callId}}"
}

###
